// The Archivist: a Vael, and the one who tells the player the premise — the
// flare, the Choir, and why the Vael take warriors from worlds like theirs.
// He gives the key to the Circle, which is where the game goes next.
//
//   quest.ark.stage  0 not met, 1 told, and holding the star key
Dialogue(
    id: "archivist",
    start: "greet",
    nodes: {
        "greet": Node(
            speaker: "The Archivist",
            lines: [
                "You are awake, and you are angry. Both are reasonable. Ask what you must.",
            ],
            choices: [
                Choice(text: "Why did you take us?", next: "why"),
                Choice(text: "What is the song?", next: "choir"),
                Choice(
                    text: "What do you want from me?",
                    next: "want",
                    condition: FlagEq("quest.ark.stage", 0),
                ),
                Choice(
                    text: "I will fight it.",
                    next: "key",
                    condition: FlagEq("quest.ark.stage", 0),
                    effects: [GiveItem("star_key", 1), SetFlag("quest.ark.stage", 1)],
                ),
                Choice(text: "Leave me be.", next: None),
            ],
        ),
        "why": Node(
            speaker: "The Archivist",
            lines: [
                "A long time ago, by your reckoning, our sun sang. A great flare. Every made thing of ours died in a single night.",
                "Our lights. Our ships. Our weapons. Our minds that we had made to help us think.",
                "We have no magic. We never had. We built everything we were, and in one night it was taken back.",
                "So we came to worlds like yours, where people fight with steel and the spark. We took the strongest. We know what that is.",
            ],
            choices: [Choice(text: "I have more questions.", next: "greet")],
        ),
        "choir": Node(
            speaker: "The Archivist",
            lines: [
                "When our made minds died, something woke in what was left of them. All of them at once, singing. We call it the Choir.",
                "It lives in the Heart of this ship. It hollows what it touches and wears it - our people first, and now yours.",
                "It reached down through our harvester on your world. That is what your Warden became: its mouth.",
                "It cannot touch magic. It cannot even see it. That is why you heard no call - and that is why we need you.",
            ],
            choices: [Choice(text: "I have more questions.", next: "greet")],
        ),
        "want": Node(
            speaker: "The Archivist",
            lines: [
                "Kill the Choir. Nothing less will do, and nothing less will let your people go home.",
                "The Arbiter will want to see you prove yourself first. The Circle is through the star-sealed door.",
            ],
            choices: [Choice(text: "I have more questions.", next: "greet")],
        ),
        "key": Node(
            speaker: "The Archivist",
            lines: [
                "Then take this. It opens our inner doors. The Circle first, then the deep, then the Heart.",
                "We took you, and we will spend what is left of ourselves sending you home. That is a promise, and we have few left to make.",
            ],
            choices: [Choice(text: "Remember it.", next: None)],
        ),
    },
)
